Shantu raster-edge feathering, local research adaptation.

The terrain texture batch loop, surface-image setup and tiled image traversal are
adapted from WorldWind Kotlin 2.1.1 (earth.worldwind:worldwind-android:2.1.1),
Copyright WorldWind Kotlin contributors, under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The upstream source classifier remains unchanged in the isolated local SDK repository.
The Apache License is retained at worldwind-labels/LICENSE.

Modifications: optional per-texture four-edge feather masks and premultiplied RGBA pair interpolation; preserve
upstream four-texture batching, shadow receiver state, pick behavior, RGB565 base
textures and cached ancestor resources. No imagery source pixels are blurred or
rewritten by this GPU effect. Conservative boundaries without a cached backing stay
opaque. This does not repair mosaics whose color discontinuities are inside a source image.
